    topicKey: "appliances-included",
    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | NE extended (session 2, whole-library generic-clause audit): generic mechanics, no NE-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with NE findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, whole-library audit): generic mechanics, already vetted against KS/NE's prohibited-lease-provisions statutes (the strictest bar found in this project to date) since this clause was already tagged KS;NE; no MN-specific statutory language or number identified in this session's statute walk that conflicts. No exculpatory/liability-waiver language present. | ND ADDED 2026-09-06 (ND re-audit, exhaustive generic-clause audit prompted by the checklist-to-CSV reconciliation screen). ND's ORIGINAL whole-library audit was written up in its log but largely never executed against the CSV -- ND was shipped 'complete' with 18 displayable LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 61-75 for CO/WY/KS/NE/MN. This row is generic boilerplate carrying no ND-specific statutory interaction; ND's ch. 47-16 was read in full from primary text this session and no conflict was identified. LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK: North Dakota has NO enumerated prohibited-lease-provisions statute (confirmed this session -- § 47-16-02 is a maximum-term cap, and § 47-16-13.3 supplies only case-by-case unconscionability). The exculpation exposure that forced fixes to this clause family in KS and NE therefore does not arise for ND, same reasoning as the WY addendum. 5a.1 JUDGMENT: UNIFORM -- states field changed, clause TEXT unchanged, no re-review owed on existing tags. | SD ADDED 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit, Tier A of the L.2 exhaustive generic-clause audit). SD displayed only 13 LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 60-75 for every other state; 46 generics had no SD tag and no SD override. Triaged per L.2, not bulk-extended. Tier A = boilerplate with no SD statutory interaction, or self-limiting text that defers to applicable law. S5a.1 JUDGMENT: adding a state tag changes `states` only - no bodyText, rule_type or content_type change - so no other tagged state's rendering is affected and NO propagation to other state logs is owed. State-driven, not uniform. CA: extended to California 2026-09-19 after re-screen against the full CA pass (the extend manifest had deferred tagging until the blocked set was resolved, and the step was then missed). No CA conflict found. CA builder note: for leases entered, amended or extended on or after 2026-01-01, a stove and refrigerator are required landlord-supplied characteristics (stove-refrigerator-ca). If the tenant opts to supply their own refrigerator, omit it from {{appliance_list}}. | NV: Read in full 2026-09-24 against NRS 118A (revisor text Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated). Applies as written. | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 (full chapter, section-open; Justia 2025 host copy with per-section history lines). Applies as written. No Texas interaction found in ch. 92. | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ conflict found. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). Generic; nothing in Part II conflicts. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | AZ: Applies as written. A.R.S. §33-1324(A)(4): landlord maintains appliances supplied or required to be supplied. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ND 2026-09-28: the LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK above is withdrawn as to any clause disclaiming liability for the landlord's own violation of law. North Dakota does have enumerated bans outside its landlord-tenant title: N.D.C.C. §§9-08-02 (exculpation), 9-08-03 (penalties), 9-08-04 (liquidated damages) and 9-08-05 (restricting enforcement). See edu-prohibited-lease-terms-nd. | GA: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. The landlord must maintain and promptly repair appliances it supplies once notified in writing, except in emergencies (N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-42(a)(4)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | SC: Tagged. Appliances present are presumed supplied by the landlord unless specifically excluded by the rental agreement, and essential-service appliances cannot be excluded (S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-440(a)(5)); opt-in exclusion row `appliances-excluded-sc`. | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). No appliance-exclusion statute (contrast SC § 27-40-440(a)(5)). TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: Maintenance of supplied appliances is a landlord duty (Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1220(A)(4)); consistent. | AL: Tagged. Landlord maintains supplied facilities and appliances in good and safe working order (Ala. Code § 35-9A-204(a)(4)). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | PA: Tagged. No statute. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed.",
