    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, CO;WY-scoping resolution): no general MN statute found conflicting with this clause's 30-day/proportional-rent-relief mechanic for ordinary failure-to-deliver-possession situations. NOTE: Minnesota does have its own narrower statute, § 504B.153, but it applies specifically to NEW CONSTRUCTION delays with a different remedy structure — that's a distinct, more specific scenario not covered by this generic clause. FLAG FOR FUTURE SESSION: consider a dedicated `possession-delay-mn` (or a conditional new-construction rider) if Steinoak wants to capture § 504B.153's specific new-construction remedy; not urgent since the generic clause doesn't conflict with it, just doesn't duplicate it. | ND extended (North Dakota session 1, same scoping review): North Dakota has no statute addressing failure to deliver possession at all (confirmed absent this session) -- no conflict, cleaner than Minnesota's case which had a narrow new-construction-specific statute to work around. | SD extended (South Dakota session 1, Title 21-16 review): SDCL 43-32-19(1) gives tenant a termination right for landlord's failure to deliver possession/repair after reasonable written request, but doesn't dictate specific lease mechanics while the tenant awaits delivery; the generic's self-limiting language is compatible. | PASS 2 CLARIFICATION (South Dakota): SDCL 43-32-19(1) gives the tenant a termination right if Landlord fails to deliver possession within a 'reasonable time after written request' - an open standard, not a fixed number of days. This generic clause's 30-day figure is a contract term the parties are free to adopt (more certain than the open statutory standard, not in conflict with it) rather than a restatement of the statute itself - cross-reference edu-tenant-termination-causes-sd for the underlying statutory right. Flagged during pass 2 to avoid confusing the two. CA: NOT extended to California - its 30-day termination window conflicts with casualty-termination-ca, which states the Civ. Code s1932(1) 'reasonable time after request' right for the same event. Replaced for CA by possession-delay-ca. | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code chs. 24, 54, 91, 92 and 301 (official statutes.capitol.texas.gov text for chs. 24/54/91/301). Applies as written. Chs. 91, 92 and 24 read in full: no Texas delivery-of-possession statute. Clause is contractual and tenant-favourable. | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ delivery-of-possession statute found in text read. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No delivery-of-possession statute in Part II (full read). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | GA: Applies as written. No Georgia failure-to-deliver-possession statute located (ch. 7 read whole; not separately searched). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. No North Carolina statute on failure to deliver possession located (Chapter 42 read whole). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). No Tennessee statute on failure to deliver possession beyond Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-303 (landlord shall deliver possession, Act counties); the rent abatement and 30-day termination are contractual and lawful. TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: Non-fault delay is contractual and lawful; willful failure to deliver is governed by Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1238 (rent abates; termination on five days' written notice with refund of prepaid rent and deposits, or suit for possession and damages). Form 200 (Rev. 07/23) § 10 uses 15 days (VA log §15). | PA: Tagged. No Pennsylvania statute on failure to deliver possession (1951 Act read whole; PA log §17); the contract term governs. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed.",
