    topicKey: "hoa-compliance",
    notes: "CO added - verified this session (statute walk + full-library audit; content itself unchanged WY added 2026-08-21 (full-library cross-check pass): generic mechanics, no CO-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with WY findings from this project. | NE extended (session 2, whole-library generic-clause audit): generic mechanics, no NE-specific statutory language or number, confirmed no conflict with NE findings from this project. | MN extended (Minnesota session, whole-library audit): generic mechanics, already vetted against KS/NE's prohibited-lease-provisions statutes (the strictest bar found in this project to date) since this clause was already tagged KS;NE; no MN-specific statutory language or number identified in this session's statute walk that conflicts. No exculpatory/liability-waiver language present. | ND ADDED 2026-09-06 (ND re-audit, exhaustive generic-clause audit prompted by the checklist-to-CSV reconciliation screen). ND's ORIGINAL whole-library audit was written up in its log but largely never executed against the CSV -- ND was shipped 'complete' with 18 displayable LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 61-75 for CO/WY/KS/NE/MN. This row is generic boilerplate carrying no ND-specific statutory interaction; ND's ch. 47-16 was read in full from primary text this session and no conflict was identified. LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK: North Dakota has NO enumerated prohibited-lease-provisions statute (confirmed this session -- § 47-16-02 is a maximum-term cap, and § 47-16-13.3 supplies only case-by-case unconscionability). The exculpation exposure that forced fixes to this clause family in KS and NE therefore does not arise for ND, same reasoning as the WY addendum. 5a.1 JUDGMENT: UNIFORM -- states field changed, clause TEXT unchanged, no re-review owed on existing tags. | SD ADDED 2026-09-07 (SD re-audit, Tier A of the L.2 exhaustive generic-clause audit). SD displayed only 13 LEASE_CLAUSE rows against 60-75 for every other state; 46 generics had no SD tag and no SD override. Triaged per L.2, not bulk-extended. Tier A = boilerplate with no SD statutory interaction, or self-limiting text that defers to applicable law. S5a.1 JUDGMENT: adding a state tag changes `states` only - no bodyText, rule_type or content_type change - so no other tagged state's rendering is affected and NO propagation to other state logs is owed. State-driven, not uniform. CA: extended to California 2026-09-19 after re-screen against the full CA pass (the extend manifest had deferred tagging until the blocked set was resolved, and the step was then missed). No CA conflict found. | NV: Read in full 2026-09-24 against NRS 118A (revisor text Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated). Applies as written. | TX: Read in full 2026-09-25 against Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 (full chapter, section-open; Justia 2025 host copy with per-section history lines). Applies as written. s92.018 bars passing through GOVERNMENTAL fines unless the tenant caused the condition; association fines are not governmental and are unaffected. | NJ: added 2026-09-26 (tag-first screen, instruction 26). No NJ conflict found. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | FL: Applies as written (tag-first screen, instruction 26). Condominium and HOA statutes (chs. 718, 720) not read. Fla. Stat. §83.64(1)(e) bars retaliation against a tenant who pays rent to an association on its demand. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | AZ: Applies as written. A.R.S. §§33-1260.01 and 33-1806.01 limit what a condominium or planned-community association may demand of a renting owner (edu-hoa-rental-rules-az). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | ND 2026-09-28: the LIABILITY-LANGUAGE CHECK above is withdrawn as to any clause disclaiming liability for the landlord's own violation of law. North Dakota does have enumerated bans outside its landlord-tenant title: N.D.C.C. §§9-08-02 (exculpation), 9-08-03 (penalties), 9-08-04 (liquidated damages) and 9-08-05 (restricting enforcement). See edu-prohibited-lease-terms-nd. | GA: Applies as written. Condominium instruments may specially assess common expenses caused by an occupant's conduct against the unit (O.C.G.A. § 44-3-80(b)(2)). No Georgia statute lets an association demand rent from a tenant located (official full-text search 2026-09-28). s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | NC: Applies as written. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | SC: Tagged. Generic; no South Carolina conflict. | TN: Tagged 2026-09-28 (section text read 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser (Justia host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code with history lines; 2025-2026 public chapters screened; TN log §1)). No conflicting statute. TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. | VA: Tagged 2026-09-28. VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read against the official Code of Virginia section-open (law.lis.virginia.gov; VA log §1). Basis: No conflicting Virginia statute. | AL: Tagged. No conflicting statute; association flag rule (Ala. Code § 35-1-5.1) binds the association, not the tenant. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed. | PA: Tagged. No statute. s5a.1: states-only change, no propagation owed.",
