  "bed-bug-disclosure-co": {
    ruleTypes: ["RECOMMENDED"],
    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-08-20",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-29",
    topicKey: "bed-bug-disclosure",
    notes: "CO: CITED — C.R.S. § 38-12-1005 (HB19-1328, ch. 426, L. 2019). RESOLVED 2026-09-13. '8 months' confirmed current, verbatim: disclosure owed 'UPON REQUEST FROM A PROSPECTIVE TENANT... WITHIN THE PREVIOUS EIGHT MONTHS.' Real duty is request-triggered/pre-lease, not an unconditional in-lease disclosure as originally framed - bodyText reworded to reflect the tenant's actual entitlement while still delivering the information in the lease. Also added a second duty the clause was missing entirely: on request, disclose the most recent bed-bug inspection date. Exact internal subsection within § 38-12-1005 still not isolated (minor - section itself is confident). (Restored 2026-09-25 from lease-clause-citations-CO.csv, which still holds the same data.) | CO: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): optional clause (Taylor's pattern 3): the duty is owed on request to a prospective tenant, before the lease; the clause records what was disclosed. Restated entitlement sentence removed. Companion education row: edu-bed-bugs-co.",
  },
  "utility-submetering-disclosure-co": {
    ruleTypes: ["CONDITIONAL"],
    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-08-18",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-29",
    topicKey: "utility-submetering-disclosure",
    notes: "CO: CITED — Disclosure duty: C.R.S. § 6-1-737(4.5)(d) (added by HB26-1013). Fee cap: § 38-12-801(3)(a)(VI).. RESOLVED 2026-09-13. Disclosure duty confirmed verbatim: one of four RUBS safe-harbor conditions at (4.5)(a)-(d) - 'THE LANDLORD CLEARLY AND CONSPICUOUSLY DISCLOSES THE METHOD OF ALLOCATION... IN A TENANT'S RENTAL AGREEMENT OR AN ADDENDUM.' New in 2026 (HB26-1013) - 'as required by Colorado law' was not accurate before this bill's effective date, is accurate now. No bodyText change needed; clause already correctly implements the disclosure + fee-cap combination described in the safe harbor. (Restored 2026-09-25 from lease-clause-citations-CO.csv, which still holds the same data.) | CO: SCRUB 2026-09-29 (checklist instruction 66, three-bucket test): kept the required method disclosure; the fee is now the landlord's stated choice, and the restated fee cap and no-markup rule are covered by edu-rubs-uncertainty-co.",
  },
