    notes: "K.S.A. 58-2554. Closes the 'broader landlord-identity-change notice' question Wyoming's log explicitly checked (edu-no-broad-identity-change-notice-wy) but this pass never circled back to for Kansas, despite having already pulled the primary text earlier in the session. Structurally different from Colorado's proactive 1-business-day tenant-notification mandate: Kansas frames this as a liability-shield for the departing landlord/manager once notice is given, not an affirmative notice duty independent of that protection. Worth flagging: this doesn't obligate the new owner/manager to notify the tenant of anything — it only protects the old one, once notice happens.",
