    topicKey: "parking",
    notes: "MN added (Minnesota session, exculpatory-clause follow-up): Minnesota has no statute voiding landlord liability-waiver language (unlike CO/KS/NE). Instead, courts apply common-law strict construction per Justice v. Marvel, LLC, 979 N.W.2d 384 (Minn. 2022), extending Dewitt v. London Rd. Rental Ctr., Inc., 910 N.W.2d 412 (Minn. 2018): a clause releasing a party from its own negligence is enforceable only if it 'clearly and unequivocally' says so; broad unqualified 'not liable' language (as in the generic clause) risks being read as failing that standard and providing no real protection. No exculpatory clause, however drafted, can bar claims for intentional, reckless, or willful/wanton conduct, so this clause carves those out explicitly rather than attempting (and failing) to cover them. Taylor reviewed and approved this draft language before it was committed to the library. GROUP NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Parking' -> 'Parking & Storage' (session drift; 12 canonical groups are used by all nine states).",
