    notes: "NV: NRS 477.140(1), read on the revisor's current ch. 477 page (Rev. 4/15/2026, 2025 session incorporated - currency established by the revisor page itself; the section's own history line not captured): the owner or operator of an apartment building with at least three dwelling units must equip each unit with a smoke detector whose placement is approved by the \"authority\" (NRS 477.100: the State Fire Marshal in counties under 100,000; the local building/fire officials in Clark and Washoe). DOES NOT REACH single-family homes, duplexes, or individually rented condos - the clause is RECOMMENDED for them and states the statutory duty only in the bracketed apartment limb. No state rule on maintenance, testing or batteries was found; the allocation here is contractual and lawful. Adopted Regulation R132-18 (eff. 2020-02-27) removed the former NAC misdemeanor for disabling a detector, so the no-disable duty now rests on this clause. Clark County (population >= 700,000): NRS 477.030(11) makes the Fire Marshal's building-code rules yield to the locally adopted International Fire/Building Codes - local layer flagged, not resolved. Carbon-monoxide alarms: no NRS or NAC requirement located (NRS 477 read; 278/461/461A not searched) - deliberately NOT in this clause. Research-pass basis: primary for the text; secondary leads discarded (a tenant-rights site asserted a statewide CO-alarm rule with no statute behind it).",
