    notes: "TX: Tex. Prop. Code ch. 92 read in full, section-open, 2026-09-25 (Justia '2025 Texas Statutes' host copy supplied by Taylor; per-section history lines checked - latest amendments 89th Leg., R.S. (2025); CONFIRMED 2026-09-25 against the official statutes.capitol.texas.gov ch. 92 page supplied by Taylor: no 1st or 2nd called-session amendment; text matches section for section - TX log s14). Controlling text: s92.008(h)-(r) (Amended by Acts 2009 (H.B. 882), eff. Jan. 1, 2010, and Acts 2013, 83rd Leg., R.S., Ch. 899 (H.B. 1086), eff. Sept. 1, 2013). This is the only lawful landlord interruption of a utility for nonpayment in ch. 92, and it requires the right to be in a written lease (s92.008(h)(1)); a reconnection fee requires the exact amount in a written lease (s92.008(r)). Everything else - dual notices with the words 'electricity termination notice' underlined or bold, delivered separately from other content; no interruption on days the landlord cannot take payment, before such days, after a 32 F day with a freeze forecast, or during/after a heat advisory; medical-certification + deferred-plan protection (63 days); energy-assistance pledge protection; 2-hour reconnection; no interruption for a prior tenant's debt, non-electric charges, 6-month-old bills or disputed bills; no eviction for the electric bill unless unpaid 2 business days after interruption - is notice/practice, in edu-lockout-utility-rules-tx. NOT the allocation-disclosure question the dormant utility-submetering-disclosure-tx row asks; that turns on Water Code / PUC rules (unread).",
