    topicKey: "security-deposit-interest",
    notes: "FL: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official 2026 Florida Statutes (flsenate.gov / leg.state.fl.us), with per-section history lines. Controlling text: Fla. Stat. §83.49(2)(a)-(d) (s. 2, ch. 2025-16 latest). Trigger: the landlord rents five or more individual dwelling units ('This subsection does not apply to any landlord who rents fewer than five individual dwelling units'). Timing: 'in the lease agreement or within 30 days after receipt'. Delivery: in person, by mail, or e-mail under §83.505. Change of depository: new notice within 30 days, except merger, rename or transfer of the institution. The capitalized disclosure is the §83.49(2)(d) text verbatim; the capitals are the statute's own (layout table, instruction 28). Failure to give the notice is not a defense to rent (§83.49(2)); any remedy is damages (§83.55). The builder should show this row when the landlord's unit count is 5+ and default it on otherwise too (harmless). topic_key shared with the NJ/OH interest-notice rows.",
