    lastChecked: "2026-09-26",
    topicKey: "notice-delivery-methods",
    notes: "FL: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official 2026 Florida Statutes (flsenate.gov / leg.state.fl.us), with per-section history lines. Controlling text: Fla. Stat. §83.505 (s. 1, ch. 2025-16, eff. 2025-07-01). Statutory form verbatim ('substantially the following form'); names are builder placeholders. Requirements: an addendum both parties sign; each provides a valid e-mail address; the addendum 'conspicuously advises' that the election is voluntary and revocable (the form's own sentences do this). Revocation and address updates by written notice, effective on delivery (§83.505(2)-(3)). E-mail notice is delivered when sent unless returned undeliverable (§83.505(4)); the sender must keep a copy and evidence of transmission (§83.505(5)); other lawful methods remain available (§83.505(6)). Florida notices that may go by e-mail under this addendum include §83.49 deposit notices, §83.50 address notices, §83.51(2)(a)1 extermination notices, and §83.56 notices. Layout (instruction 28): separate addendum; conspicuous voluntariness statement. topic_key shared with electronic-notice-consent-tx.",
