    notes: "FL: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official 2026 Florida Statutes (flsenate.gov / leg.state.fl.us), with per-section history lines. Controlling text: Fla. Stat. §83.535 (s. 5, ch. 93-255): 'No landlord may prohibit a tenant from using a flotation bedding system' that meets building codes; the tenant 'shall be required to carry' flotation insurance in the tenant's name, standard in the industry, in a reasonable amount, with a loss payable clause to the owner. Opt-in landlord right (instruction 30): the insurance condition is written as something the landlord requires, so the lease should state it. Companion to common-area-use-fl (FL-only override; Taylor declined a shared edit 2026-09-26). {{flotation_insurance_amount}} must be reasonable; the statute sets no figure. topic_key shared with waterbed-ca.",
