    topicKey: "radon-disclosure",
    notes: "FL: Primary text pasted by Taylor 2026-09-26 from flsenate.gov/Laws/Statutes/2026 (official 2026 Florida Statutes), read section-open with history lines. Controlling text: Fla. Stat. §404.056(5) (history ends s. 297, ch. 2011-142): the notification 'shall be provided on at least one document, form, or application executed at the time of, or prior to, ... execution of a rental agreement for any building' and 'shall contain the following language' (verbatim above). Exception: residential transient occupancy under Fla. Stat. §509.013(12) of 45 days or less (not read; L.5 dependency). No testing duty for rentals (mandatory testing in §404.056(4) covers schools, 24-hour care facilities and day care centers only). Layout and timing (instruction 28): exact statutory language, on a document executed at or before signing; the lease qualifies. No sanction stated in §404.056(5). Builder: include in every FL lease unless the term is transient and 45 days or less. topic_key shared with radon-disclosure-co.",
