    notes: "AZ: Read section-open 2026-09-26/27 in the browser from azleg.gov (official legislative compilation, stated as updated through the 57th Legislature, 2nd Regular Session, 2026). azleg ARS pages print no history lines, so currency rests on the compilation date and the session-law check in the AZ log (s1.1). Controlling text: A.R.S. §33-1318(A) (written notice; mutually agreed release date within 30 days; protective order under §13-3602 or law-enforcement departmental report), (B) (name and address request), (C) (30-day look-back unless waived), (D) (liability through termination; prepaid rent for the month retained; deposit not withheld for the early termination), (E)-(F) (lock at tenant's cost; rekey or replace; landlord may keep a key and refuse one to the named person), (G) (no access for the served respondent unless escorted by law enforcement), (H) (treble damages against a tenant convicted of a false report or order), (I) (named person civilly liable to the landlord for economic losses incl. unpaid rent, fees, repairs), (J) (co-tenants), (K) (protective order applies to the whole rental property), (L) (unrelated terminations preserved), (M) (good-faith immunity); §33-1318.01 (law enforcement officer; injunction against harassment under §12-1809; repay concessions; 'law enforcement officer' per §38-1101). RECOMMENDED, not REQUIRED (Taylor confirmed 2026-09-27): the statute gives the right regardless of lease text and does not require it to be stated. STATUTE WATCH, flagged for Claude CLI: add A.R.S. §§33-1318 and 33-1318.01 to the legal-watch list; if Arizona amends them to require lease or notice text (as several library states do), move this row to REQUIRED. L.5 dependency §13-3601 resolved by the research pass 2026-09-27 (read from azleg.gov): 'domestic violence' is a listed offense (incl. threatening, §13-1202, and sexual assault, §13-1406) committed within a listed relationship - marriage or former marriage, current or former co-residence, a child in common, pregnancy by the other party, specified blood, in-law or court-order relationships, a child in the household, or a current or former romantic or sexual relationship (§13-3601(A)). A threat by a stranger is NOT domestic violence; the separate sexual-assault prong (in the dwelling) has no relationship element. 'As Arizona law defines it' in the clause carries this. Still NOT read: §§13-1406, 13-3602, 12-1809, 38-1101. The sexual-assault right is limited to an assault 'in the tenant's dwelling'; domestic violence has no location limit. Landlord remedies (H)-(I) belong in education (edu-landlord-remedies-after-breach-az). | AZ close-out 2026-09-27: Laws 2026, ch. 242 amended §13-3602 (orders of protection), which §33-1318(A)(1) incorporates by reference; §33-1318 itself was not amended 2024-2026 (full-text scan). §13-3602 not read (L.5); the clause does not restate its content.",
