    contentType: "LEASE_CLAUSE",
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-09-27",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-27",
    topicKey: "landlord-disclosure",
    notes: "WY added 2026-09-27, gap-discovery source 2 (WY log section 20.1). Opt-out clause under W.S. 1-21-1201(a)(i), verified section-open: \"'Owner' means the owner, lessor or sublessor of a residential rental unit and for purposes of notice and other communication required or allowed under this article, 'owner' includes a managing agent, leasing agent or resident manager UNLESS THE AGENT OR MANAGER SPECIFIES OTHERWISE IN WRITING IN THE RENTAL AGREEMENT.\" The statutory default is that the agent IS the owner for notice purposes; the only way to vary it is lease text, so this is an instruction 30 opt-in/opt-out right that a silent lease forfeits. CONDITIONAL: include only where an agent or manager is involved AND the landlord wants notices delivered to the landlord directly. Omit it and the agent remains a valid recipient of every notice and demand under Article 12. Surfaced by the ASUW Approved Lease's signature block, which asks the lessor to identify capacity (owner, agent, or holder of a leasehold). Companion education row: edu-agent-capacity-notice-wy.",
