    notes: "NC: Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from the official General Statutes on ncleg.gov (Chapter 42 read whole on the chapter page, which prints each section's history line; the latest amendments in those history lines are S.L. 2025-45, 2025-52 and 2025-54; all 61 session laws of 2026 (S.L. 2026-1 to 2026-61) screened for Chapter 42 amendments, none found). Instruction 24 family closed for NC: supersedes the blank-states parent `security-deposit-return` (M.11). Controlling text: N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-52 (itemize and mail or deliver with the balance 'no later than 30 days after termination of the tenancy and delivery of possession of the premises to the landlord'; interim accounting within 30 days and final within 60 days if the claim cannot be determined; unknown address: apply after 30 days and hold the balance 'for at least six months'; no withholding for normal wear and tear; no retention above actual damages) (history: 1977, c. 914; 2009-279); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-54 (on termination of the landlord's interest 'by sale, assignment, death, appointment of receiver or otherwise', within 30 days transfer the deposit to the successor and notify the tenant by mail, or return it; either relieves the landlord). Remedies: N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-55 (civil action for accounting and recovery; willful failure to account and refund voids the right to retain any portion; attorney's fees for willful noncompliance). No statutory move-in or move-out inspection procedure (edu-no-move-in-inspection-rule-nc). Unclaimed balances: Chapter 116B not read beyond N.C. Gen. Stat. § 116B-53 (edu-security-deposit-rules-nc).",
