    effectiveFrom: "2026-09-28",
    lastChecked: "2026-09-28",
    topicKey: "waiver-by-acceptance",
    notes: "NC: Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from the official General Statutes on ncleg.gov (Chapter 42 read whole on the chapter page, which prints each section's history line; the latest amendments in those history lines are S.L. 2025-45, 2025-52 and 2025-54; all 61 session laws of 2026 (S.L. 2026-1 to 2026-61) screened for Chapter 42 amendments, none found). OPT-IN LANDLORD RIGHT (instruction 30): N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-26(c) ('In an action for ejectment based upon N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-26(a)(2), the lease may provide that the landlord's acceptance of partial rent or partial housing subsidy payment does not waive the tenant's breach for which the right of reentry was reserved, and the landlord's exercise of such a provision does not constitute a violation of Chapter 75') (added by S.L. 2011-252; history ends 2012-17). Without the lease provision the default rule on waiver by acceptance is case law, not relied on. Separate statutory rule, no lease text needed: collecting rent with knowledge of illegal acts under Article 7 is not a waiver (N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-73).",
