    notes: "SC: Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from the official South Carolina Code of Laws on scstatehouse.gov (Title 27, Chapter 40 read whole on its chapter page with every history line; the site states the Code is current through the 2025 session; the full text of every 2025 act (Act Nos. 1 to 94) and every 2026 act (Act Nos. 95 to 274) was screened for Chapter 40, Chapter 37 and landlord-tenant terms; SC log §1). Controlling text: S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(a) (unexplained absence for fifteen days after default in rent 'must be construed as abandonment'); S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(b) (voluntary utility termination plus unexplained absence after default: abandonment immediate); S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(c) (duty to make reasonable efforts to re-rent at a fair rental; lease ends at the new tenancy; if no reasonable efforts or abandonment accepted as surrender, lease terminated as of the date the landlord has notice of the abandonment; periodic tenancies treated as a month or week); S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(d) (after abandonment or end of the agreement, where the tenant removed a substantial portion of property or voluntarily and permanently terminated utilities, property with a fair-market value of $500 or less may be disposed of, using forcible entry if required); S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(e) (otherwise removal only under S.C. Code Ann. § 27-37-10 to S.C. Code Ann. § 27-37-150); S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-730(f) (no liability for property over $500 disposed of under (d) unless grossly negligent) (1995 Act No. 112). Post-eviction property placed on the street: S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-710(D) (`edu-eviction-process-sc`). A contractual lien on household goods is unenforceable (S.C. Code Ann. § 27-40-740(a)). Supports the tagged `surrender-end-of-term`.",
