    topicKey: "pet-policy",
    notes: "TN: TN-SCOPE: STATEWIDE TEXT. Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser from Justia's host copy of the 2025 Tennessee Code (the official code is published by LexisNexis), with each section's history line; currency checked against the full text of every public chapter of the 114th General Assembly (2025 and 2026 Pub. Ch. 1 to 1142 and the seven 2025 First Extraordinary Session acts, publications.tnsosfiles.com) and against the LexisNexis Tennessee Code Unannotated free public access site, which already prints the 2026 Pub. Ch. 606 sections (TN log §1). WHY THE SHARED pet-policy IS NOT TAGGED: (1) its unqualified promise to 'indemnify Landlord from claims arising from Tenant's pet(s)' reaches claims resting on Landlord's own liability, which Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-203(a)(2) makes unenforceable in Act counties, and § 66-28-203(b) gives the tenant actual damages where a landlord willfully uses a lease containing terms known to be prohibited (instruction 49); (2) its right to 'enter the property and remove a pet, without liability' is not among the entries Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-403(e) allows (emergency and a deceased or incapacitated tenant are; a sick pet is not). Text adapted from pet-policy-sc with 'Tennessee law' for 'South Carolina law' and the Tennessee 'support animal' term. No Tennessee statute caps pet deposits, pet rent or pet fees (LexisNexis '(pet w/10 deposit) or \"pet fee\" or \"pet rent\"': 0 hits; TN log §17); the only limits are for service, support and guide animals (assistance-animal-accommodation-tn). COUNTY-LAYER PILOT (Taylor, 2026-09-28): Tennessee is the test case for the future county/local layer. The URLTA (Tenn. Code Ann. Title 66, Chapter 28) applies only in the 17 counties over 75,000 people in the 2010 census, a list frozen by 2021 Pub. Ch. 182 § 2 (Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-102(a)): Anderson, Blount, Bradley, Davidson, Hamilton, Knox, Madison, Maury, Montgomery, Rutherford, Sevier, Shelby, Sullivan, Sumner, Washington, Williamson and Wilson.",
