    notes: "VA: VA-SCOPE: STATEWIDE. Read section-open 2026-09-28 in the built-in browser on the official Code of Virginia (law.lis.virginia.gov; Title 55.1 Chapter 12 read whole from the vacodefull page, which prints the 2026-session amendments and every delayed-effective version with its history line); 2024-2026 amending chapters read in enrolled text on lis.virginia.gov with their effective-date clauses (VA log §1). Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1226 (history ends 2023, cc. 433, 434; not amended 2024-2026): (A) cap 'two months' periodic rent'; four permitted uses; itemized written notice with any amount due 'within 45 days after the termination date of the tenancy or the date the tenant vacates the dwelling unit, whichever occurs last'; early termination or improper notice lets the landlord retain against actual damages but still requires the 45-day disposition notice; (B) one check to all tenants unless each agrees otherwise in writing, forwarding address, hold in escrow, State Treasurer after one year; (C) no immediate credit against delinquent rent; utility withholding only after the advance notice in a termination notice, a vacating-date confirmation or a separate notice at least 15 days before disposition, then written confirmation and balance within 10 days; (E) in-tenancy deductions noticed within 30 days; third-party contractor notice within 45 days plus 15 more days to itemize (the Virginia REALTORS Form 200, Rev. 07/23, still says 30 more days; VA log §15); willful failure = return of deposit plus actual damages and fees; successor holder bound; (F) two years of deduction records open to the tenant; (G) move-out inspection notice and 72-hour inspection; (H) one deposit where there is an assignee or sublessee. Va. Code Ann. § 55.1-1200 ('Security deposit' includes a pet deposit; money is an application deposit until the commencement date); Va. Code Ann. §§ 55.1-1206(C), 55.1-1208(A)(7) (deposit plus damage and renter's insurance premiums paid before commencement capped at two months' rent; a lease provision exceeding it is prohibited). No interest is owed (edu-no-deposit-interest-va). INSTRUCTION 24 (REQUIRED family, parent row blank): closed by this VA override of security-deposit-return; the parent is not tagged. Optional expedited disposition fee: expedited-deposit-disposition-va. Timing and damage-insurance rules: edu-security-deposit-rules-va.",
